      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-algebra-2003-p2.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "1\n\nIf we multiply top and bottom by \\(\\cos ^{2}\\left(20^{\\circ}\\right)\\), the numerator becomes \\(\\sin ^{2}\\left(20^{\\circ}\\right) \\cdot(1-\\) \\(\\left.\\cos ^{2} 20^{\\circ}\\right)=\\sin ^{4}\\left(20^{\\circ}\\right)\\), while the denominator becomes \\(\\sin ^{4}\\left(20^{\\circ}\\right)\\) also. So they are equal, and the ratio is 1 .",
